					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-241363#post-783163</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-241363/the-king-is-dead#post-783163</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 13 May 2010 16:55:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Josef Kald</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>382782</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Alas, poor Kondraki! I knew him, Gears: a fellow<br /> of infinite jest, of most excellent fancy: he hath<br /> caused me to smile a thousand times; and now, how<br /> abhorred in my imagination it is! my gorge rims at<br /> it. Here hangs this genius that I have admired I know<br /> not how oft. Where be your gibes now? your<br /> gambols? your 408? your flashes of merriment,<br /> that were wont to set the channel on a roar? Not one<br /> now, to mock your own grinning? quite chap-fallen?<br /> Now get you to Rights' chamber, and tell her, let<br /> her draw a pencil thick, to this favour she must<br /> come; make her laugh at that.</p> <p>I liked this story, nonetheless. Upvoted.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
